SUMMARY="Go compiler, standard library and tools for Haiku ARM64"
DESCRIPTION="Native Go 1.27.4 toolchain for Haiku ARM64 (go, gofmt, the standard \
library source, and the compile/link/asm/cgo/vet/cover/fix tool binaries), cross-built \
with scripts/cross-arm64-golang.sh against a from-scratch RenkuOS/Go haiku/arm64 \
runtime port -- this image had no prior Go support of any kind, and HaikuPorts has no \
arm64 repository to depend on either. GOROOT is self-contained under lib/go; bin/gofmt \
is a plain symlink into it, the same layout rust_bin uses for cargo/rustc. Revision 4 \
made bin/go a wrapper instead (the real binary moved to lib/go/bin/go-real), fixing two \
things found building a real third-party web app: (1) this toolchain shipped with both \
GOPROXY and GOSUMDB blank, so every module fetch failed outright (\"GOPROXY list is not \
the empty string, but contains no entries\" / \"missing GOSUMDB\") until a user set them \
by hand -- the wrapper now defaults both, same as a real Go install would, without \
overriding a caller that already set them. (2) github.com/gin-gonic/gin (the most-used Go \
web framework) failed to build at all: its default logger calls into \
github.com/mattn/go-isatty, which ships one real/stub IsTerminal implementation per OS \
family and has none that matches haiku, so IsTerminal/IsCygwinTerminal were undefined at \
compile time -- confirmed building a real gin.Default() app with the vanilla module. \
Fixed by adding haiku to the existing \"unsupported platform, just return false\" stub \
(isatty_others.go, same safe default already used for js/wasm/appengine/tinygo/nacl -- \
correct here too, since a terminal-color check over an SSH-piped session should say \"not \
a terminal\" anyway) and shipping the patched module, repackaged at the same path and \
version, as a local GOPROXY-protocol override directory the wrapper puts ahead of the \
real proxy in GOPROXY. Revision 5 adds the same treatment for golang.org/x/sys, which \
has no haiku support in any published version at all, breaking any module that imports \
golang.org/x/sys/unix directly (a far larger share of the ecosystem than go-isatty's own \
gap) -- ported from korli/go's own sibling fork korli/sys_haiku (its master-haiku branch, \
amd64 only) plus this port's own already-existing arm64 extension of the same files \
(cmd/vendor/golang.org/x/sys/unix/*_arm64* in this port's own src/ tree), applied onto a \
clean v0.50.0 checkout. GONOSUMDB covers both overridden modules, since their content \
deliberately differs from the public checksum database. See \
scripts/golang-goproxy-overrides/README.md for both patches and how to extend this to \
another module with the same kind of gap. Confirmed end to end from a clean module cache: \
fresh go mod init, go get github.com/gin-gonic/gin, go build, run, and a real HTTP 200 \
from curl against a gin.Default() handler; separately, a small program built against the \
patched x/sys/unix tree and run on the real target machine over SSH, exercising Stat, a \
full Socket/Bind/Getsockname round trip, and IoctlGetTermios -- no manual replace \
directive, no pre-seeded cache, just this package's own defaults. Also confirmed, on the \
same real, already-installed -4 package over plain SSH (no desktop session): a clean-cache \
\`go build std\` (the entire standard library, many real fork/execs) using the package's \
own native bin/haiku_arm64/go to build itself, exit 0, ~52s."
HOMEPAGE="https://go.dev/"
VERSION="1.27.4"
REVISION="5"
LICENSE="BSD (3-clause)"
COPYRIGHT="2009 The Go Authors"
ARCHITECTURES_SUPPORTED="arm64"

PROVIDES="golang_bin = $VERSION
cmd:go = $VERSION
cmd:gofmt = $VERSION"
REQUIRES="haiku"

# Provenance of the upstream source this was built from -- not a
# haikuporter SOURCE_URI/CHECKSUM_SHA256 this recipe can actually be
# built with (see NOTE below), but the exact same values HaikuPorts'
# own dev-lang/golang recipe uses for the x86_64 build, confirmed by
# downloading and hashing this URL directly: the arm64 runtime port in
# this port's own src/ tree is applied on top of exactly this tree, not
# a different one.
SOURCE_URI="https://github.com/korli/go/archive/go1.27.4-haiku.tar.gz"
SOURCE_DIR="go-go1.27.4-haiku"
CHECKSUM_SHA256="f3d5c413020820a685800a5d665212661db14889e852ace571599ab28cc8fde1"

NOTE="cross-built, not haikuporter-built: see scripts/cross-arm64-golang.sh for how \
the .hpkg under prebuilt/arm64/ was produced. SOURCE_URI/CHECKSUM_SHA256 above are \
provenance only (what korli/go source this port's own src/ files were applied onto), \
not something haikuporter can actually build from with a plain BUILD()/INSTALL(): the \
arm64 runtime port itself (the files under this repo's own src/, copied on top of that \
source tree file for file) and the host-vs-native dual-toolchain build \
(GOOS=haiku GOARCH=arm64 ./make.bash against a linux/arm64 bootstrap compiler, run inside \
the project's own haiku-builder Docker container) aren't expressible in that format."

PREBUILT_PACKAGES="pkgman-repo/prebuilt/arm64/golang_bin-$VERSION-$REVISION-arm64.hpkg"
